ow East Kalimantan, Indonesia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/berber-dahir"><span class="enc-name">Berber Dahir</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berber Dahir was a decree issued on 16 May 1930 in the name of Sultan Muhammad V under the French protectorate in Morocco.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berber-languages"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berber-languages.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berber languages</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berber languages, also called Tamazight, are a branch of the Afroasiatic family spoken by the Amazigh peoples of North Africa, from Morocco and Algeria to Libya…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berber-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berber-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berber Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 739–743 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berber Revolt was a series of uprisings in North Africa between 739 and 743 CE against the rule of the Umayyad Caliphate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berbera"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berbera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berbera</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Berbera is a port city on the Gulf of Aden in Somaliland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/berbers"><span class="enc-name">Berbers</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berbers, or Amazigh, are the indigenous peoples of North Africa, living across the Maghreb and the Sahara.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berchtesgaden"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/im