rth-eastern Spain, known from Livy's account of the campaign of Cato the Elder in 195 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bergpark-wilhelmshohe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bergpark-wilhelmshohe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bergpark Wilhelmshöhe</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Bergpark Wilhelmshöhe is a large landscape park on a hillside west of Kassel, Germany, laid out by the landgraves of Hesse-Kassel from the late 17th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bergslagen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bergslagen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Bergslagen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Bergslagen is a historic mining region in central Sweden, stretching across parts of Dalarna, Västmanland, Örebro and Värmland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/bergueda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bergueda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berguedà</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berguedà is a comarca, or county, in the province of Barcelona in Catalonia, Spain, covering the upper valley of the Llobregat with Berga as its capital.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/berisades"><span class="enc-name">Berisades</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Berisades was one of the three kings among whom the Odrysian Kingdom was divided after the murder of Cotys I in 360 BCE, ruling the western part towards the Strymon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berke"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berke</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Berke was khan of the Golden Horde from 1257 to 1266, a grandson of Genghis Khan through Jochi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berkshire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berkshire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berkshire</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Berkshire is a county in southern England, west of London, with Reading as its largest town.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berkyaruq"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berkyaruq.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berkyaruq</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Berkyaruq was sultan of the Great Seljuk Empire from 1094 to 1105, the eldest son of Malik Shah.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berleburg-bible"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berleburg-bible.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berleburg Bible</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berleburg Bible is an eight-volume German Bible translation with a mystical and allegorical commentary, published at Berleburg from 1726 to 1742.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/berleburg-castle"><span class="enc-name">Berleburg Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Berleburg Castle is a palace in Bad Berleburg in the Wittgenstein region of Westphalia, Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berlin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berlin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berlin</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Berlin is the capital and largest city of Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berlin-airlift"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berlin-airlift.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berlin Airlift</span><span class="enc-type">Crisis · 1948–1949</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berlin Airlift was the supply of West Berlin by air in 1948–1949, after the Soviet Union blockaded road, rail and canal access to the city's western sectors in June…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berlin-conference"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berlin-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berlin Conference</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1884–1885</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berlin Conference was a meeting of European powers and the United States convened by Otto von Bismarck from November 1884 to February 1885.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berlin-declaration-1945"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berlin-declaration-1945.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berlin Declaration (1945)</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berlin Declaration of 5 June 1945 was issued by the four Allied commanders, Eisenhower, Zhukov, Montgomery and de Lattre de Tassigny, after Germany's unconditional…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berlin-wall.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berlin Wall</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berlin Wall was a guarded barrier built by the German Democratic Republic from 13 August 1961 to cut off West Berlin and stop East Germans fleeing to the West.</span></a></li></ul>
